  "summary": "A flywheel is a heavy rotating wheel that stores kinetic energy (E = ½ I ω²). In this crank press the motor slowly keeps the flywheel spinning; when the punch strikes, the flywheel gives up some energy and slows down a little, delivering a much larger peak power than the motor alone could. Between strokes the motor brings it back up to speed. Flywheels also smooth the uneven torque of engines.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Mechanical energy storage",
    "type": "Spoked cast-iron flywheel on a crank press"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "animation": "Flywheel slows briefly at each punch stroke and recovers",
    "rim": "Most of the mass at the rim → high inertia"
  },
